 n←cid MySQLExec q;sql;binds;c;r
⍝ Run a statement that doesn't return rows: INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, CREATE …
⍝ Returns the number of rows affected.
⍝
⍝   db MySQLExec 'CREATE TABLE notes (id INT, txt VARCHAR(100))'
⍝   db MySQLExec 'INSERT INTO notes VALUES (:1<I:, :2<C100:)' 1 'hello'
⍝   db MySQLExec 'UPDATE notes SET txt=:1<C100: WHERE id=:2<I:' 'hi' 1

 (sql binds)←{1≥|≡⍵:⍵ ⍬ ⋄ (⊃⍵)(1↓⍵)}q
 c←2⊃#.SQA.CursorName cid
 :If 0=⊃r←#.SQA.Prepare c sql
     r←#.SQA.Exec(⊂c),binds
 :EndIf
 {}#.SQA.Close c
 :If 0≠⊃r
     ⎕SIGNAL⊂('EN' 11)('Message'('MySQLExec: ',⍕3⊃r))
 :EndIf
 n←{1<≢⍵:2⊃⍵ ⋄ 0}r
